{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And as for you.</b> Rabbi Solomon [Rashi] said: טרם תיראון is like לא תיראון, and similarly טרם ישכבו (Genesis 19:4). But this word does not occur as he supposed, for the matter always follows it: after טרם ישכבו it is written \"the men of the city, the men of Sodom, surrounded the house,\" and the sense is: when the time of their lying down arrived, they surrounded the house. Likewise, טרם יקראו ואני אענה (Isaiah 65:24), and likewise בטרם יקטירון את החלב (Psalms 115 [?]). Thus is every טרם, and so טרם is not like לא. The Gaon [Saadia] attached the matter, and explained thus: Moses said to Pharaoh, I will pray to remove the plague of hail — only what is destroyed is destroyed."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The citation ש\"אב is likely a corruption; Ibn Ezra appears to cite Psalms 115, but the verse about the fat portions and incense does not match any standard psalm verse exactly. Translated hyper-literally as the Hebrew letters stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:04.621676968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}